blocks.english:
Ignatius consecrates himself to the crown of Mars;
Bellona at Pamplona broke his hope of this favour.
Scarcely healed, he thinks of entering the ways of life;
[The printed “Quasi rite Divos, lecitavit, renuncians avitae” is unresolved.]
He leaves his father’s hearths, and [printed plensuque charitatis: unresolved form],
Everywhere plants the seed [printed salubrae sanctitatis: unresolved qualifier] of holiness.

blocks.originalPreparedEnglish:
Ignatius consecrates himself to the crown of Mars;
Bellona at Pamplona broke his hope of this favour.
Scarcely healed, he thinks of entering the ways of life;
[The printed “Quasi rite Divos, lecitavit, renuncians avitae” is unresolved.]
He leaves his father’s hearths, and, full of charity,
Everywhere plants the seed of saving holiness.

blocks.english:
At the altar of the Virgin Mother [printed pernoct: unresolved shortened form] he endures in prayer;
He tends his heart, cleansing it from every stain of sin.
He tames the flesh by fasts and austerities;
[The printed “Insensu, et cupidis et laetitiis quibusque” is unresolved.]
He has often experienced outward labours;
He has often experienced inward sorrows.

blocks.originalPreparedEnglish:
At the altar of the Virgin Mother he endures through the night in prayer;
He tends his heart, cleansing it from every stain of sin.
He tames the flesh by fasts and austerities;
[The printed “Insensu, et cupidis et laetitiis quibusque” is unresolved.]
He has often experienced outward labours;
He has often experienced inward sorrows.

blocks.english:
At thirty years of age, [the printed “imaestatis” is unresolved], he is a beginner in Latin;
To this he is driven by an unusual ardour of charity.
[The printed “Et actus inde nobis sodalium sequella” is unresolved.]
That he might devote himself to affairs, a fruitful remedy for mortals.
He bore calumnies, words, [the printed “saenasque” is unresolved], and prisons;
And more willingly endures wounds [the printed “necque” is unresolved].

